# The shapes, the text, the states and the properties — fifteen pictures from
# four test sources, in one suite, compared byte for byte.
#
# `a_card_is_painted_and_compared/` beside this is the smallest whole
# lifecycle. This one is the *range*: the ends of every axis a snapshot has.
#
#   * **The tree.** Nothing at all, one run of text, a hundred stacks deep, a
#     thousand siblings, and three lists that differ only by what marks their
#     items — none, discs, numbers — because a marker is the one thing painted
#     beside a box rather than on it.
#   * **The text.** Marks that combine onto the letter before them, characters
#     no bundled face has a glyph for, a run that reads right to left, and a
#     line wider than the page — wrapped, and refusing to wrap.
#   * **The state.** All five of them, over one tree that paints differently in
#     each, so five goldens that have to differ from one another.
#   * **The properties.** Every one the painter honours, at zero and at the
#     viewport's own size, in both tiers — the classes the compiler extracted
#     and the declarations it could not.
#
# **Fifteen goldens, and they are the assertion.** They were recorded by the
# copy-and-patch backend on a mac and CI compares them on Linux too, so this
# directory is where "the same tree paints the same bytes on both hosts" is
# claimed for text shaping rather than for boxes: `снимок.png` is the one
# picture here that a shaper disagreeing with itself across two platforms would
# move.
#
# The snapshot named `снимок` is also the name edge case. A snapshot names a
# file, and that name is not ASCII; it is spelled in a script with no
# decomposable characters on purpose, because the two hosts do not agree about
# what to do with a combining mark in a *file name*.
#
# Four test sources and one `test/__snapshots__`, which is the other claim here:
# a suite's sources are one binary, and a snapshot from the fourth file lands
# beside a snapshot from the first.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs.

doc: "every tree shape, every state and every property the painter honours, painted and compared against fifteen goldens, with the whole record-and-fail lifecycle over them"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/scenes", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "pass.txt"
}

# Nothing was written: a run that matched leaves no diff image behind.
path { path: "lib/scenes/test/__snapshots__/empty.diff.png"  exists: false }

# A snapshot nobody has recorded yet fails, and the report says how to record
# one rather than showing a difference against nothing.
edit {
  file: "lib/scenes/test/shapes.buri"
  replace: "snapshot(ctx, \"empty\", ui.nothing(), .Hover);"
  with: "snapshot(ctx, \"never-recorded\", ui.nothing(), .Hover);"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/scenes", "--force"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "missing.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/scenes/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: false }

# `--update` records the one that was missing and rewrites the fourteen that
# already matched, and the run after it compares against what it just wrote.
run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/scenes", "--update", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "recorded.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/scenes/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: true }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/scenes", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "again.txt"
}

# The negative twin: two words of one tree, the five state snapshots that show
# it, and the diff images on disk beside their goldens.
edit {
  file: "lib/scenes/test/states.buri"
  replace: "ui.text(.Const(\"beside it\")),"
  with: "ui.text(.Const(\"beside them\")),"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/scenes", "--force"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "changed.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/scenes/test/__snapshots__/state-hover.diff.png"  exists: true }
path { path: "lib/scenes/test/__snapshots__/state-checked.diff.png"  exists: true }
path { path: "lib/scenes/test/__snapshots__/empty.diff.png"  exists: false }
